---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { limits, site } from '../config';
---

<Layout title="Privacy policy | Slug" description="What Slug collects, why, and who it is shared with.">
  <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
  <p class="post-meta">Last updated November 16, 2026</p>

  <p>
    Slug runs batch inference: you send prompts, we run them and return the results. This page says what we collect
    when you use slugllm.com and the Slug API, what we do with it, and who else handles it.
  </p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Account details.</strong> Your email address and, if you set one, a password, which is stored hashed. If
      you sign in with Google or GitHub, we receive your email address, name and profile picture from them. We don't
      get access to anything else in those accounts.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>API keys.</strong> The name you give each key, when it was made and last used, and a hash of the key. We
      don't keep the key itself.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>What you send through the API.</strong> The prompts in your batches and the outputs we generate for
      them.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Usage and logs.</strong> How many requests and tokens you use, plus the technical logs any web service
      keeps, such as IP address, browser and time of request.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>The site sets only the storage it needs to keep you signed in. We don't run advertising or tracking cookies.</p>

  <h2>What we use it for</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Running your batches and returning the results.</li>
    <li>Signing you in, and sending account email such as sign-up confirmation and password resets.</li>
    <li>Measuring usage for limits and billing.</li>
    <li>Keeping the service working and secure, and investigating abuse.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We don't sell your data, and we don't use your prompts or outputs to train models.</p>

  <h2>Who else handles it</h2>
  <p>We use other companies to run Slug, and they process data for us:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Supabase, for accounts and our database.</li>
    <li>Vercel, for hosting this website.</li>
    <li>Amazon Web Services and Google Cloud, for running inference and sending account email.</li>
    <li>Google and GitHub, if you choose to sign in with them.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We also share data when the law requires it, or if Slug is acquired or merged, as part of that deal.</p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    Batch outputs can be downloaded for {limits.outputLinkDays} days after a batch finishes. We keep account details
    and usage records for as long as your account is open, and logs for a limited time. When you ask us to delete your
    account, we delete your account details and API keys, and keep only what we need for legal or billing reasons.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask for a copy of your data, ask us to correct it, or ask us to delete your account by emailing
    <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>. You can revoke API keys yourself from your
    <a href="/account/">account page</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>Slug is not meant for anyone under 13, and we don't knowingly collect their data.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>If we change this policy we will update this page and the date at the top.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about privacy: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.</p>
</Layout>
